<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35688" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνίζ-ω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to set in,</i>
			
				Ep.
			
			aor. 1
			
				Med.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνεείσατο</span> he <i>placed upon,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρύμνῃ κούρην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.188
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> intr., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνιζάνω</span>
			, pf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνίζηκα,</span>
			<i>sit in</i> or <i>on,</i> c.acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάκους ἐνίζουσαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					1108
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), prob. in <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				801
			</span></i> (lyr.): c. dat., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σώματι καὶ ψυχῇ . . ἐνίζει Ἔρως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					196b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεῦρα τοῖς μυσὶν -ηκότα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					2.691
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ -ηκυῖα τοῖς μορίοις ποιότης τοῦ
					φαρμάκου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					11.354
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς ἕψημα τῶν βοτανῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aret.
					<u>CA</u>
					2.8
				</span></i>
			.</div>
